# `.codegen` must never be committed

- Do **not** stage, commit, or push `.codegen/` (or any vendored `zero_codegen` tree under it).
- `.codegen/` is local tooling only; it is listed in `.gitignore`.
- If asked to commit and `.codegen` appears in status, leave it untracked — never force-add it.
- Teammates obtain the codegen tool by copying from the scaffold or an approved local source; it is not part of the GitHub history for this product.
